Skip tsystem.h's fallback `extern int errno` on MakaOS.

MakaOS's <errno.h> declares errno as `extern __thread int errno;` (a
thread-local variable, not a macro), so gcc/tsystem.h's `#ifndef errno`
guard does not skip its plain `extern int errno;` fallback -- which then
collides with the thread-local declaration and breaks the libgcc build
(needed for a hosted libstdc++). errno is already declared by the
<errno.h> included just above, so the fallback is redundant on MakaOS.

(A proper POSIX errno-as-macro fix would trip the guard without this
patch, but that renames the errno symbol and requires re-porting the
whole userland; deferred -- see docs/VIRGL_BRINGUP.md.)

Signed-off-by: MakaOS <noreply@makaos>

diff --git a/gcc/tsystem.h b/gcc/tsystem.h
--- a/gcc/tsystem.h
+++ b/gcc/tsystem.h
@@ -100,8 +100,12 @@
 /* All systems have this header.  */
 #include <errno.h>

-#ifndef errno
+/* MakaOS's <errno.h> (included just above) declares errno as a thread-local
+   `extern __thread int errno;` rather than a macro, so the usual `#ifndef
+   errno` guard would not skip this fallback and the plain `extern int errno;`
+   would collide with the thread-local one.  errno is already declared. */
+#if !defined(errno) && !defined(__makaos__)
 extern int errno;
 #endif

 /* If these system headers do not exist, fixincludes must create them.  */
